#X text 240 83 Works with sound files: reads file info and loads them
into arrays. Various formats are supported. Supports array name patterns.;
#X text 240 138 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 163 • Loading samples and loops into arrays — bringing
external audio files into a patch as Pd arrays \, ready for playback
with [tabplay~] \, [tabread4~] or processing with other array-based
objects.;
#X text 250 233 • Multi-channel file handling — loading multi-channel
files into multiple arrays at once using array name patterns \, for
example array_[1-4] for a 4-channel file \, or array_[left|right] for
stereo.;
